  "puzzleGuideThemeTitle": "Puzzles by theme",
  "puzzleGuideTrainingGoal": "Find the best move in every puzzle, one after another.",
  "puzzleGuideTrainingRule1": "Puzzles are picked to match your rating: the better you do, the harder they get.",
  "puzzleGuideTrainingRule2": "Move the right piece: if the move is correct your opponent replies and it's your turn again; if it's wrong, it's taken back.",
  "puzzleGuideTrainingRule3": "On a new puzzle, solving it on the first try raises your rating; if you make a mistake or look at the solution it counts as failed, your rating drops and the puzzle goes back into review. Puzzles you've already seen don't change your rating.",
  "puzzleGuideTrainingRule4": "The hint costs you nothing: it circles the piece to move.",
  "puzzleGuideTrainingRule5": "There's no clock and no limit on mistakes: you can stop whenever you like.",
  "puzzleGuideThemeGoal": "Train a single tactical pattern: every puzzle has the same theme.",
  "puzzleGuideThemeRule1": "Move the right piece: if the move is correct your opponent replies; if it's wrong, it's taken back.",
  "puzzleGuideThemeRule2": "On a new puzzle, solving it on the first try raises your rating; with mistakes or a revealed solution it counts as failed, your rating drops and the puzzle goes back into review.",
  "puzzleGuideThemeRule3": "There's no clock and no limit on mistakes.",
  "puzzleGuideDailyGoal": "Solve today's puzzle: it's the same all day long.",
  "puzzleGuideDailyRule1": "Find the right sequence of moves: if you get one wrong it's taken back and you can try again.",
  "puzzleGuideDailyRule2": "With “Try again” you start over from the initial position, with “Solution” you see the moves.",
  "puzzleGuideDailyRule3": "It only counts as solved if you make no mistakes and don't look at the solution; otherwise it counts as failed.",
  "puzzleGuideDailyRule4": "A new one arrives tomorrow.",
  "puzzleGuideReviewGoal": "Find the solutions to the puzzles you got wrong.",
  "puzzleGuideReviewRule1": "Each puzzle comes back at growing intervals (1, 3, 7, 14 and 30 days): today you only get the ones that are due.",
  "puzzleGuideReviewRule2": "If you solve it without mistakes the interval gets longer; if you slip, it starts again from one day.",
  "puzzleGuideReviewRule3": "Review doesn't change your training rating.",
  "puzzleGuideReviewRule4": "Once today's puzzles are done, there's nothing left to do.",
  "puzzleGuideRunBase1": "The puzzles get harder as you go.",
  "puzzleGuideRunBase2": "Every solved puzzle is worth 1 point.",
  "puzzleGuideRunTail1": "Your personal best is saved for each mode.",
  "puzzleGuideRunTail2": "You can leave whenever you like: the points and XP you earned still count.",
  "puzzleGuideStormGoal": "Solve as many puzzles as you can in {minutes} minutes.",
  "puzzleGuideStormRule1": "A mistake costs {seconds} seconds, resets your combo and moves on to the next puzzle.",
  "puzzleGuideStormRule2": "With 5, 12, 20 and 30 puzzles in a row you gain 3, 5, 7 and 10 seconds (then 10 for every 10 puzzles).",
  "puzzleGuideStormRule3": "There are no lives: the run ends when time runs out.",
  "puzzleGuideRushGoal": "Solve as many puzzles as you can in {minutes} minutes, with three lives.",
  "puzzleGuideLivesRule1": "A mistake costs you a life and moves on to the next puzzle.",
